# 8. REQUIRED EXTREME-SPEED ANIMATION TESTING

This is one of the most important parts of this update.

Do not just test the boss animations while walking slowly.

Test the procedural animation system at normal speed, high speed, and maximum REVENANT speed.

### Test scenarios

Test every spider-legged boss and REVENANT variant in the following situations:

1. Standing still.
2. Walking slowly.
3. Running at normal speed.
4. Running at high speed.
5. Running at maximum speed.
6. Accelerating from a complete stop.
7. Decelerating from maximum speed.
8. Making sharp 90-degree turns.
9. Performing sudden 180-degree turns.
10. Dashing while moving.
11. Chasing a moving player.
12. Repositioning during combat.
13. Moving across uneven terrain.
14. Colliding with obstacles.
15. Transitioning from running into an attack.
16. Transitioning from an attack back into running.
17. Landing after a jump or leap.
18. Fighting while multiple nearby units are also moving at high speed.

### Specific animation failures to look for

Check for:
- Legs stretching beyond their intended lengths.
- Feet floating above the ground.
- Feet clipping into the ground.
- Feet sliding excessively.
- Legs crossing through the body.
- Joints suddenly snapping.
- Limbs moving in the wrong direction.
- Gait cycles slowing down while the body speeds up.
- Gait cycles continuing after the boss stops.
- Body movement becoming disconnected from leg movement.
- IK instability during rapid turns.
- Animation jitter caused by physics update timing.
- Excessive body bouncing.
- Leg targets jumping between positions.
- Animations breaking when several bosses are active.

### Required acceptance criteria

The animation system must:

- Maintain stable joint constraints.
- Keep the feet reasonably synchronized with the ground.
- Maintain consistent leg segment lengths.
- Adapt to actual movement speed.
- Transition smoothly between movement states.
- Avoid visible snapping and jitter.
- Remain stable at the maximum intended movement speed.
- Continue working when several high-speed bosses or REVENANTS are active.

Test the actual maximum speeds used by the buffed REVENANTS, not just the old boss speed values.

If an animation breaks at the new maximum speed, fix the underlying calculation and repeat the test.

**Do not reduce REVENANT movement speed merely to hide an animation problem.**

